#### verses ####
1:1-1 marker=/1/23/1 start=/1/16 end=/1/29/1 "BOOK I\nPsalms 1–41\nThe Two Paths\nBlessed is the man\nwho does not walk in the counsel of the wicked,\nor set foot on the path of sinners,\nor sit in the seat of mockers."
1:2-2 marker=/1/31/1 start=/1/29/2 end=/1/33/1 "But his delight is in the Law of the LORD,\nand on His law he meditates day and night."
1:3-3 marker=/1/35/1 start=/1/33/2 end=/1/41/1 "He is like a tree planted by streams of water,\nyielding its fruit in season,\nwhose leaf does not wither,\nand who prospers in all he does."
1:4-4 marker=/1/45/1 start=/1/41/2 end=/1/47/1 "Not so the wicked!\nFor they are like chaff driven off by the wind."
1:5-5 marker=/1/49/1 start=/1/47/2 end=/1/51/1 "Therefore the wicked will not stand in the judgment,\nnor sinners in the assembly of the righteous."
1:6-6 marker=/1/55/1 start=/1/51/2 end=/1/57/1 "For the LORD guards the path of the righteous,\nbut the way of the wicked will perish."
2:1-1 marker=/1/65/1 start=/1/62 end=/1/67/1 "The Triumphant Messiah\nWhy do the nations rage [2:1 Or noisily assemble; see Revelation 11:18.]\nand the peoples plot in vain?"
2:2-2 marker=/1/69/1 start=/1/67/2 end=/1/75/2 "The kings of the earth take their stand\nand the rulers gather together,\nagainst the LORD\nand against His Anointed One: [2:2 Cited in Acts 4:25–26]"
2:3-3 marker=/1/77/1 start=/1/75/3 end=/1/79/1 "“Let us break Their chains\nand cast away Their cords.”"
2:4-4 marker=/1/83/1 start=/1/79/2 end=/1/85/1 "The One enthroned in heaven laughs;\nthe Lord taunts them."
2:5-5 marker=/1/87/1 start=/1/85/2 end=/1/89/1 "Then He rebukes them in His anger,\nand terrifies them in His fury:"
2:6-6 marker=/1/91/1 start=/1/89/2 end=/1/93/1 "“I have installed My King on Zion,\nupon My holy mountain.”"
2:7-7 marker=/1/97/1 start=/1/93/2 end=/1/103/2 "I will proclaim the decree\nspoken to Me by the LORD:\n“You are My Son;\ntoday I have become Your Father. [2:7 Literally today I have begotten You; cited in Acts 13:33, Hebrews 1:5, and Hebrews 5:5]"
2:8-8 marker=/1/105/1 start=/1/103/3 end=/1/107/1 "Ask Me, and I will make the nations Your inheritance,\nthe ends of the earth Your possession."
2:9-9 marker=/1/109/1 start=/1/107/2 end=/1/111/3 "You will break them [2:9 LXX You will rule them or You will shepherd them] with an iron scepter;\nYou will shatter them like pottery. [2:9 Cited in Revelation 2:27; see also Revelation 12:5 and Revelation 19:15.]”"
2:10-10 marker=/1/115/1 start=/1/111/4 end=/1/117/1 "Therefore be wise, O kings;\nbe admonished, O judges of the earth."
2:11-11 marker=/1/119/1 start=/1/117/2 end=/1/121/1 "Serve the LORD with fear,\nand rejoice with trembling."
2:12-12 marker=/1/123/1 start=/1/121/2 end=/1/131/1 "Kiss the Son, lest He be angry\nand you perish in your rebellion,\nwhen His wrath ignites in an instant.\n\nBlessed are all who take refuge in Him."
3:1-1 marker=/1/139/1 start=/1/136 end=/1/145/1 "Deliver Me, O LORD!\nA Psalm of David, when he fled from his son Absalom.\n\nO LORD, how my foes have increased!\nHow many rise up against me!"
3:2-2 marker=/1/147/1 start=/1/145/2 end=/1/151/2 "Many say of me,\n“God will not deliver him.”\nSelah [3:2 Selah or Interlude is probably a musical or literary term; here and throughout the Psalms.]"
3:3-3 marker=/1/153/1 start=/1/151/3 end=/1/155/1 "But You, O LORD, are a shield around me,\nmy glory, and the One who lifts my head."
3:4-4 marker=/1/157/1 start=/1/155/2 end=/1/161/1 "To the LORD I cry aloud,\nand He answers me from His holy mountain.\nSelah"
3:5-5 marker=/1/163/1 start=/1/161/2 end=/1/165/1 "I lie down and sleep;\nI wake again, for the LORD sustains me."
3:6-6 marker=/1/167/1 start=/1/165/2 end=/1/169/1 "I will not fear the myriads\nset against me on every side."
3:7-7 marker=/1/173/1 start=/1/169/2 end=/1/179/1 "Arise, O LORD!\nSave me, O my God!\nStrike all my enemies on the jaw;\nbreak the teeth of the wicked."
3:8-8 marker=/1/181/1 start=/1/179/2 end=/1/185/1 "Salvation belongs to the LORD;\nmay Your blessing be on Your people.\nSelah"
